      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T09:29:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e if you need a flag then make use of Kconfig to know which all platform would make use of such BBRAM feature for charge limit.\n\nCurrently this feature is enabled per platform according to the KCONFIG flag `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_CONTROL_PERSIST_TO_BBRAM`, please refer to  crrev/c/8424843 for the flag usage. \n\n\u003e This region is very precious and we don\u0027t need to exhaust it by using upper/lower and flag.\n\nStoring the lower, upper, and flag values requires 3 bytes to ensure the full runtime configuration set by the OS/ADSP is maintained across reboots. On NPCX, this utilizes 3 of the 79 available bytes in the 128-byte BBRAM, whereas other ECs generally have 60-80% of their BBRAM capacity unused.\n\nAlthough removing the `flag` option might save space, it would complicate the initialization process needed to restore the proper BBRAM values if the flag deviates from `normal` mode. Furthermore, this approach necessitates a thorough examination of all potential edge cases.",
      "parentUuid": "21b58795_5154e30b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "29876c6f26acce268738f6c93018da53f36f8a7f",
